From 03101cc21304ab55510b5127b35f1a734ca64e68 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jay Leaton <58495321+jayleaton@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 10 Oct 2026 10:42:56 +0700
Subject: [PATCH 18/60] Session memory for paged-KV families: page pool, prefix
 trie, RAM residency budget, streamed NVMe tier.

zig/src/sessions keeps a chat's KV pages after its request ends: entries are found by a trie over chained page
digests, held in RAM within a residency budget (chats and pool bytes), and the least recently used idle chat is
parked to an NVMe tier and streamed back on resume. Ranks that split KV run every store call in the same order, so
their books stay identical. It complements core/prompt_cache, which snapshots a whole family state; a family that
uses it reports the resident bytes as Memory.cache and its budget as Info.prompt_cache_plan. No family uses it yet;
zig build test-sessions runs the host tests, the NVMe tier on real files.

(cherry picked from commit 05c5213a6934a6f11249a738b0903cec58c7bbb8)
